ine features to a new chart-studio package.\r\n\r\n# Steps to reproduce\r\nWhat are the steps we should take to reproduce the bug:\r\n1. Import plotly.express as px\r\n\r\n## Expected behavior:\r\nPlotly should be imported for use with st.plotly_chart()\r\n\r\n## Actual behavior:\r\nPlotly is unable to be imported.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot from 2019-09-16 10-26-12](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6628275/64979382-773c0300-d86c-11e9-92b4-39fd81b7fb01.png)\r\n\r\n## Is this a regression?\r\nFunctions as expected with plotly 3.10.\r\n\r\n# Debug info\r\n- Streamlit version: 0.45.0\r\n- Python version: 3.7.4\r\n- Using Conda\r\n- OS version: Ubuntu 19.04\r\n- Browser version: Chrome 77.0.3865.75 \r\n\r\n# Additional information\r\nNot the end of the world as 3.10 is still working; was curious if there is a way to include the necessary version of plotly as a dependency somewhere.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"j4th","id":6628275,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MjgyNzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6628275?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th","html_url":"https://github.com/j4th","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j4th/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/streamlit/streamlit/issues/112/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"http